.TH OTPME-CA 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-ca \- manage OTPme certificate authorities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-ca
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIca\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-ca
manages certificate authorities (CAs) in the OTPme system. CAs issue and manage X.509 certificates for nodes and hosts, maintain certificate revocation lists (CRLs), and provide the PKI infrastructure for secure communication between OTPme components.
.PP
Each CA generates a self-signed CA certificate with configurable X.509 distinguished name fields. CAs can issue server, client, node, and host certificates. CRL data is propagated to all nodes in the realm.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS CA Management
.TP
.B add \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIca\fR
Create a new CA with a self-signed certificate.
.TP
.B del \fIca\fR
Delete a CA.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIca\fR]
Display CA information. Without arguments, shows all CAs.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List CAs, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fIca\fR
Enable a disabled CA.
.TP
.B disable \fIca\fR
Disable a CA without deleting it.
.TP
.B touch \fIca\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Certificate Operations
.TP
.B dump_cert \fIca\fR
Export the CA certificate to stdout.
.TP
.B dump_key \fR[\fB\-p\fR \fIpassphrase\fR] \fIca\fR
Export the CA private key to stdout. Use \fB\-p\fR to encrypt with a passphrase.
.TP
.B dump_ca_chain \fIca\fR
Export the CA certificate chain to stdout.
.TP
.B create_client_cert \fR[\fIX.509 options\fR] \fIca\fR \fIcn\fR \fIcert_out_file\fR \fIkey_out_file\fR
Create a client certificate signed by the CA and write it to \fIcert_out_file\fR/\fIkey_out_file\fR. Used for non-OTPme hosts that need to authenticate against \fBbackupd\fR; see \fBBACKUP_CLIENT_CERT\fR in
.BR otpme.conf (5).
The X.509 options are the same as for
.B add
(\fB\-\-country\fR, \fB\-\-state\fR, \fB\-\-locality\fR, \fB\-\-organization\fR, \fB\-\-ou\fR, \fB\-\-email\fR, \fB\-\-valid\fR, \fB\-\-key\-len\fR).
.SS CRL Management
.TP
.B crl_validity \fIca\fR \fIdays\fR
Set CRL validity period in days.
.TP
.B dump_crl \fIca\fR
Export the certificate revocation list to stdout.
.TP
.B update_crl \fIca\fR
Remove outdated certificates from the CRL.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] \fIca\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set a configuration parameter. Use \fB\-d\fR to delete (reset to default) or \fB\-a\fR to append the value to a list-typed parameter.
.TP
.B show_config \fIca\fR [\fIparameter\fR]
Show all configuration parameters.
.TP
.B get_config \fIca\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show the value of a single configuration parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIca\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set CA description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIca\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIca\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Object Changelog
Every change to the object writes an entry: who made it, when, and what was done.
A change can carry a comment of its own, through the global option \fB\-\-changelog\fR.
.PP
An \fIentry_id\fR is the number the listing shows in front of an entry, counted from 0.
.PP
Only the comment of an entry can be changed or removed.
What was done and by whom stays as it is.
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B changelog \fIca\fR
Show the changelog of the CA.
Needs the ACL \fBview:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIca\fR \fIentry_id\fR \fIcomment\fR
Set the comment of that entry, or replace the one it has.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIca\fR \fIentry_id\fR
Remove the comment of that entry.
The entry itself stays, and an entry without a comment is refused.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIca\fR
Remove every entry of the changelog.
.br
This needs more than the ACL \fBclear:changelog\fR: the config parameter
.B allow_changelog_clearing
has to allow it (see \fBotpme\fR(7)).
It is true by default, but where no value is found at all, clearing is refused.
OTPme asks the token you are signed in with first, then the object.
.SS Policy Management
A \fIpolicy\fR is the name of a policy, not a path.
It is looked for in the site of the CA.
Which policies there are, and what each of them does, is in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
.PP
Attaching and detaching ask before they change anything; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B add_policy \fIca\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the CA.
.br
A policy has a list of object types it is for; one that does not name \fBca\fR is refused.
So is a second policy of a type that allows only one per object.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBassign:policy\fR.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIca\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the CA.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBremove:policy\fR, and that one verbatim: a plain \fBremove\fR does not cover it.
Detaching a policy takes away what it enforces, so it must not be cheaper than attaching one.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIca\fR
List the policies attached to the CA.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
Use \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to list only policies of the given types; these are policy types, not policy names.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBview:policies\fR.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIca\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIca\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B list_acls \fIca\fR
Display all ACLs for the CA.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIca\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIca\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIca\fR
Export CA configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIca\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS CA Creation Options
.TP
.B \-\-country \fICOUNTRY\fR
Set X.509 country field.
.TP
.B \-\-state \fISTATE\fR
Set X.509 state field.
.TP
.B \-\-locality \fILOCALITY\fR
Set X.509 locality field.
.TP
.B \-\-organization \fIORG\fR
Set X.509 organization field.
.TP
.B \-\-ou \fIOU\fR
Set X.509 organizational unit field.
.TP
.B \-\-email \fIEMAIL\fR
Set X.509 email field.
.TP
.B \-\-valid \fIDAYS\fR
CA certificate validity in days.
.TP
.B \-\-key\-len \fIBITS\fR
Key length for CA certificate in bits.
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all CAs (across all units).
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH CONFIG PARAMETERS
Configuration parameters can be set with the \fBconfig\fR command and displayed with \fBshow_config\fR.
For a complete description of all available parameters and their applicable object types, see
.BR otpme (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Creating a CA
.TP
.B otpme-ca add myca
Create a new CA with default settings
.TP
.B otpme-ca add \-\-key\-len 4096 \-\-valid 3650 \-\-country DE \-\-organization "Example Corp" myca
Create CA with specific key length, validity, and X.509 fields
.SS Certificate and CRL Operations
.TP
.B otpme-ca dump_cert myca
Export CA certificate
.TP
.B otpme-ca dump_key \-p mysecret myca
Export CA private key encrypted with passphrase
.TP
.B otpme-ca dump_ca_chain myca
Export certificate chain
.TP
.B otpme-ca crl_validity myca 365
Set CRL validity to 365 days
.TP
.B otpme-ca dump_crl myca
Export CRL
.TP
.B otpme-ca update_crl myca
Remove expired certificates from CRL
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
